
This is a small hack I created to allow content providers on our web server
to see who is looking at their files on the web server. Well not really,
becaus you can only see what machine is connected and now what user.
Anyway, this might take lots of hacking if you are not running your web
server on a unix machine. It has an HTML file that acts as a front end
(customize this to your taste). There is also a PERL script to put in
your cgi-bin directory. You will certainly have to change LOGDIR, and you
will want to customize the HTML output. Finally, there is also a shell
script that I run just before midnight every night that grabs just this
month's entries and creates a separate log file. It also greps out our
own site and also graphics files as we are not interested in those. Modify
so that it works for what you want to do. Variable should be set to where
your files are.
 
